Security: Update the bundled rclone binary to upstream v1.75.2

The bundled rclone v1.75.1 is built with go1.26.8 and golang.org/x/net
v0.57.0. Go advisories published on 2026-10-08 turned the scan red with three
new HIGH findings against it: CVE-2026-78667 (Range header parsing in
net/http's file server), CVE-2026-97031 (ECH extension handling in a crypto/tls
server) and CVE-2026-78669 (an HTTP/2 SETTINGS flood that also affects
clients). It also still carried CVE-2026-84445, the gRPC-Go denial of service
accepted with an expiry date because no rclone release had the fix.

We've updated the binary to the official upstream release v1.75.2. It is built
with go1.26.9 and vendors golang.org/x/net v0.60.0 and the fixed
google.golang.org/grpc pseudo-version, which clears all four findings. That
leaves .trivyignore.yaml with no accepted vulnerabilities.

`rclone sync -v` output for the exact flag set this app passes, plain and with
--no-check-certificate, is identical between v1.75.1 and v1.75.2, so the
migration's log-level check is unaffected.

